    "question": "How did Alberta health insurance coverage change between the 1970s and 1990s?",
    "scope": "pilot"
   },
   "text": "This answer was generated for a story question that assumed a change in coverage, and it is shown unedited. Its second and third sentences cite page 116 of the 1998-99 statistical supplement, not page 117, the page the story pins. Page 116 is the summary of Alberta Blue Cross non-group coverage: free for seniors 65 and over, their spouses and dependents, and some widows and widowers, available to residents under 65 as supplementary insurance, and covering items such as private or semi-private hospital accommodation, some prescription drugs and ambulance services. Page 117 counts who was enrolled in that program in 1998-99. Neither page describes the basic provincial plan the 1974 record refers to, so the answer's two halves do not describe the same program."
  }
